### Session 5 IPL: middleware, the query string, params and body together.
### The server prints one line per request (the logger middleware). Watch the terminal.

### ---- Middleware: POST /members ----

### Register a member with JSON (201)
POST http://localhost:3000/members
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Aisha Rahman", "emailAddr": "aisha@example.com", "branchNo": 1 }

### The same member as a form (201). Use this in Postman as x-www-form-urlencoded,
### NOT form-data (form-data is multipart, and req.body stays empty).
POST http://localhost:3000/members
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

name=Aisha Rahman&emailAddr=aisha@example.com&branchNo=1

### Not an email: validate() answers 400 before the controller runs
POST http://localhost:3000/members
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Aisha Rahman", "emailAddr": "not-an-email" }

### A branch that does not exist: the foreign key refuses it (400)
POST http://localhost:3000/members
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Aisha Rahman", "emailAddr": "aisha@example.com", "branchNo": 99 }

### ---- Searching with the query string: GET /books ----
### Every key is optional. Leave one out and it does not filter.

### No query string: the first 10 books, sorted by title (200)
GET http://localhost:3000/books

### Title contains "all", fiction only
GET http://localhost:3000/books?title=the&bookCat=F

### Page 2 of 3 per page, newest first
GET http://localhost:3000/books?limit=3&page=2&sort=year&order=desc

### limit is capped at 50 (400)
GET http://localhost:3000/books?limit=500

### Sort is a whitelist, so this cannot reach the SQL (400)
GET http://localhost:3000/books?sort=Title;DROP TABLE Book

### ---- Params and body together: POST /books/:isbn/copies ----
### The ISBN is in the URL. The copy number and rate are in the body.

### Add copy 4 of Charlotte's Web (201)
POST http://localhost:3000/books/0064410935/copies
Content-Type: application/json

{ "copyNo": 4, "rentalRate": 7.50 }

### The same copy again: that copy number is taken (409)
POST http://localhost:3000/books/0064410935/copies
Content-Type: application/json

{ "copyNo": 4, "rentalRate": 7.50 }

### A book that does not exist (404)
POST http://localhost:3000/books/0000000000/copies
Content-Type: application/json

{ "copyNo": 1, "rentalRate": 7.50 }

### Rate below the 2.50 minimum (400)
POST http://localhost:3000/books/0064410935/copies
Content-Type: application/json

{ "copyNo": 5, "rentalRate": 1.00 }

### ---- Mixed Practice Circuit solutions (this branch only) ----

### Station 1: POST /authors with validation (201, then 409 the second time)
POST http://localhost:3000/authors
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": 901, "name": "Sample Author" }

### Station 2: optional name filter and paging
GET http://localhost:3000/authors?name=john&limit=5

### Station 3: link an existing author to an existing book (201, then 409)
POST http://localhost:3000/books/0064410935/authors
Content-Type: application/json

{ "authorId": 2 }

### Station 4: a new book and a new author in one transaction (201)
POST http://localhost:3000/books/with-new-author
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isbn": "0000000030",
  "title": "Circuit Training",
  "yearPublish": "2026",
  "publisherId": 1,
  "bookCat": "NF",
  "authorId": 902,
  "authorName": "Tan Wei Ling"
}
